            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_a8b2e206">B5:Coll.004</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_f5efae11" xml:lang="de">Neue Freymäurer-Lieder, mit bequemen Melodien</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_7d9c5f74">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_d8b580fa">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_c9f28253">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_c72cbff0">
               <date isodate="1749" xml:id="date_59d89598">1749</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_fa847033">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_12301ef5">
               <p xml:id="idm86">In 1746 Scheibe joined the recently established Masonic Lodge, Zorobabel, and a couple of months later four other musicians also became members. They were most likely asked to join so that music could be played at their meetings. Among other members of the Masons was <persName xml:id="idm87" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Elias Schlegel</persName>, a close acquaintance of Scheibe’s. In late June 1748, that is after he had been dismissed as Kapellmeister, Scheibe sought permission to dedicate a collection of songs with a figured bass to the Masons – a permission that he received. The following year Scheibe had composed sixteen songs and issued them as <rend xml:id="idm88" fontstyle="italic">Neue Freymäurer-Lieder</rend> with an extensive introduction explaining the reason for composing the new songs. He mentions that to accomplish a greater variety in performance, he arranged many of the songs so that they include both solo and chorus sections; and the melodies are light and easy and comfortable for all throats and voices (‘Hälsen und Stimmen’) so that everybody, trained as well as untrained in music, are able to join in singing. In 1750 Scheibe included a brief list of corrections to the Freymäurer-edition in his foreword to his translation of <persName xml:id="idm89" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Ludvig Holberg</persName>'s <rend xml:id="idm90" fontstyle="italic">Peter Paars ein comisches Heldengedicht</rend> (SchW C4:011). In 1776 Scheibe published a new collection in which he included the present songs, many of which were revised (SchW B5:Coll.006).</p>
            </history>
